# bootstrap/PROVENANCE — provenance for the bootstrap/teko.c currently committed to this tree.
#
# RESEED (hand-harvest, isolated worktree, forward-only) — §16-FASE4 FS + TIME + RUSAGE
# (expurgo/f4-fs-env-time-random, D90). Migra as pernas de filesystem, relógio e pico de RSS do
# teko.c emitido do FFI teko_rt.c para syscall intrínseco (Linux) / extern fn por-target
# (macOS libSystem, Windows kernel32), zerando o libc dessas pernas no objeto do teko.c:
#   1. FS -> syscall (src/fs/fs.tks, por #os): list_dir sobre SYS_getdents64 (buffer + parse dos
#      registros linux_dirent64 por offset em Teko, ordenacao byte-lexicografica out-of-place para
#      um walk reproduzivel), mkdir sobre SYS_mkdirat, remove_file sobre SYS_unlinkat, is_dir/stat
#      sobre SYS_statx. macOS: libSystem opendir/readdir/closedir/mkdir/unlink/stat. Windows:
#      kernel32 FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA/FindClose/CreateDirectoryA/DeleteFileA/
#      GetFileAttributesA (buffer WIN32_FIND_DATAA cru, cFileName no offset 44). O codegen perde os
#      shortcuts host-ffi de list_dir/mkdir/remove_file (agora fns Teko user-declared).
#   2. TIME -> SYS_clock_gettime (src/time/time.tks, por #os): wall_days/wall_ns_of_day/monotonic_ns
#      sobre CLOCK_REALTIME/CLOCK_MONOTONIC (Linux syscall2; macOS clock_gettime libSystem; Windows
#      GetSystemTimePreciseAsFileTime + QueryPerformanceCounter/Frequency). localtime segue
#      civil_from_days puro (ja em Teko). journal.tks e project.tks passam a chamar
#      teko::time::monotonic_ns (saem os externs tk_rt_monotonic_ns). wall_offset_minutes (offset de
#      fuso = base de dados TZ) fica em teko_rt.c — fora do escopo civil-calendar deste bite.
#   3. RUSAGE -> SYS_getrusage (src/runtime/rtio.tks): peak_rss le ru_maxrss (offset 32) via
#      getrusage (Linux syscall2; macOS getrusage libSystem; Windows 0); cur_rss le /proc/self/statm
#      por SYS_openat/SYS_read/SYS_close. O intrinseco `peak_rss` do codegen/lower e o extern cur_rss
#      (codegen.tks, project.tks) reroteiam para teko::runtime::peak_rss/cur_rss (saem tk_peak_rss/
#      tk_cur_rss do emit do C-backend; o native leg mantem os simbolos C ate o SWEEP).
#   4. SYS consts (src/sys/sys.tks): numeros de syscall #arch-split (getdents64/mkdirat/unlinkat/
#      getrusage/chdir/getcwd, x86_64 + arm64) + O_DIRECTORY/STATX_BASIC_STATS/S_IF*/RUSAGE_SELF +
#      extern type Statx por-#os (R3, layout de statx fixado pela fixture sys_stat_size via ref_word).
#   - PROVA ZERO-LIBC: nm -u do objeto do teko.c emitido (clang -std=c2x -c) NAO lista open/openat/
#     stat/statx/mkdir/opendir/readdir/closedir/getrusage/fopen/getcwd/chdir/unlink indefinidos; os
#     externs tk_rt_list_dir/mkdir/remove_file/wall_days/wall_ns_of_day/monotonic e tk_peak_rss/
#     tk_cur_rss sairam do emit. Restam tk_rt_getenv/setenv/getcwd/chdir (env: deferido) e
#     tk_rt_wall_offset_minutes (TZ: deferido) — ambos ainda satisfeitos por teko_rt.c.
#   - FIXPOINT: gen2.c == gen3.c byte-identico; reproducao gen0(bootstrap)->gen1.c == bootstrap/teko.c.
#   - Fixtures (examples/regressions/): sys_openat_read, sys_getdents, sys_stat_size, localtime_civil,
#     sys_getrusage_rss — todas exit 0 sob o gen2.
#
# O DEGRAU (bootstrap/DEGRAU) segue declarado: o release publicado nao compila esta arvore.
